  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226602/assets/ec1381a50c493fce0f5017e706251c68c1a8a20ba5b68ef268d5905aa20772e6.png)\n\nThe circles $r=4\\sqrt{2}$ and $r=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ intersect at points $A$ and $B,$ as shown above. What are the polar coordinates $(r,\\theta )$ of the point $A?$ Express the polar angle $\\theta \\in [{0}^{∘},\\text{ }\\,{360}^{∘})$ in degrees.\n\n$(r,\\theta )=(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘})$",
